  "status": "RUNG LABELS AS K0 INDICES. (T1) the cubic module's 6 signed axes present the free abelian group of rank 3 with 3 relations (the opposite pairs) and no torsion; the icosahedral star's 12 signed directions are Q-independent inside Q(sqrt 5)^3, presenting rank 6 with 6 relations and no torsion - the exact form of the density V214 measured by shortest elements, and the reason no finite Brillouin zone exists on it. (T2) the labels therefore live in different groups: K0 = wedge^even Z^r has rank 4 for the cubic module and 32 for the star, of which 4 and 16 classes are representable by cycles of degree at most 2 in three dimensions. (T3) the two ladders count differently in a way that is not a convention: the closed-word return probability falls as n^(-r/2), measured slopes -1.4848 (r2 1.000000) against -2.9719 (r2 1.000000) on exact integers up to n = 60, the two count forms agreeing at every length. (T4) the census ladder crosses 1/(16 pi) at n = 10 (cubic) and n = 4 (star): single-digit rungs, nowhere near 208; and the family count that supplies the coefficient's factor 3 doubles to 6 on the star. VERDICT: the ladder's algebra moves with the module - rank 3 to 6, K0 Z^4 to Z^32, return exponent -3/2 to -3 - while the published n* = 208 and coefficient 2.710 live on the traced-link Cartan-norm estimator of V203/V204, a statement about the clock and the link algebra that the module change leaves untouched (the internal sector carrying it is unchanged, V217). Nothing in the published ladder arithmetic moves; what moves is the ladder the star module would have to build for itself, and V218 showed its dynamical half cannot be resolved at n = 208: (832)^6 = 3.3e+17 diagonalisations of a 128-dimensional step on the six-torus.",
